hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"957","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever enters Paradise will always remain in blessings and prosperity, he will never be miserable, his clothes will never become old, nor will his youth ever end, and in Paradise there is that which no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has ever imagined."""
"958","It is narrated from Qatadah, may Allah have mercy on him, regarding the statement of Allah Almighty: ""long shade,"" he said: Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""In Paradise, there is a tree under whose shade a rider can travel for a hundred years, but he will not be able to reach its end."" Mu'ammar said: Muhammad bin Ziyad informed me that he heard Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrate the same from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. Then Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: If you wish, recite the statement of Allah Almighty: ""And extended shade."""
"959","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""In Paradise, there is a tree under whose shade a rider can travel for a hundred years."""
"960","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The people of Hell will be cast into Hell, and it will say, 'Are there any more?' until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, comes to it and places His foot in it, then it will contract and say, 'Enough, enough.'"""
"961","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The first group from my Ummah to enter Paradise will be in the form of the moon on the fourteenth night, then those who enter after them will be in the form of the brightest star in the sky. They will neither need to relieve themselves nor spit nor blow their noses. Their combs will be of gold and their sweat will be musk. Their incense burners will be of aloeswood (oud). Their wives will be houris, and their creation will be in one form, like their father Adam (peace be upon him), sixty cubits tall."""
"962","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When a servant seeks refuge from Hell seven times, it says: 'O Lord! Your such-and-such servant has sought refuge from me, so grant him refuge.' And whoever asks Allah for Paradise seven times, Paradise says: 'O Lord! Your such-and-such servant has asked concerning me, so admit him (to me).'"""
"963","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Of the things from Paradise on earth, only this stone (the Black Stone) and the planting of the Ajwa date palm remain; the vessels of Paradise are immersed in the water of the Euphrates three times a day. A man asked: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? He replied: Then what concern do I have if I did not hear it from him? He asked again, and he replied: Then what concern do I have if I did not hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"
"964","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The fire that people kindle is one part out of seventy parts of the fire of Hell.” They said: O Messenger of Allah! This alone would be sufficient. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “It has been increased by sixty-nine degrees.”"
"965","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""This fire of yours is one seventieth part of the fire of Hell. If water had not been poured on it seven times, mankind would not have been able to benefit from it."""
"966","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""We are the last to come in the world, but on the Day of Resurrection we will be the first. The first group of my Ummah to enter Paradise will be seventy thousand individuals who will have no reckoning. Each of their faces will shine like the full moon of the fourteenth night. Then those who come after them will shine like the brightest star in the sky, and then after that, they will be in ranks, one after another."""
"967","Ibn Abi Khalid narrated with this chain the same narration."
"968","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: “Send blessings upon me, for your sending blessings upon me is a means of purification for you, and ask Allah to grant me al-Wasilah.” The narrator stated: He (peace be upon him) was asked about al-Wasilah, or he informed them about it, and said: “It is a high rank in Paradise, only one person will attain it, and I hope that I will be that person.”"
"969","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Send blessings upon me, for it is purity for you, and ask Allah to grant me al-Wasilah, for it is a high rank in Paradise, which only one man will attain, and I hope that I will be that man."""
"970","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! I seek refuge with You from hunger, for it is a bad companion, and I seek refuge with You from betrayal, for it is a bad confidant or he said a bad sign."""
"971","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! How is Paradise constructed?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""One brick is of gold and one brick is of silver, its mortar is of musk, its soil is saffron, its pebbles are pearls. Whoever enters it will be happy and will not be disappointed, his clothing will not wear out, nor will his youth decline."""
"972","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was asked: Will (men) have intercourse with the women of Paradise? He replied: Yes, with such a private part that will never tire, such a private part that will never wear out, and such a desire that will never end."
"973","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: It was asked from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): Will the people of Paradise have intercourse with their wives? So he (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes, with such a private part that will not tire, such a private part that will not wear out, and such desire that will not end."""
"974","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Muhammad (peace be upon him), tell me, Paradise whose width is equal to the heavens and the earth, then where will Hell be? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Tell me, this night which has covered everything for you, what will become of it?"" He said: Allah knows best. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah does whatever He wills."""
"975","It is narrated with the same (previous) chain, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever enters Paradise will be in the form of Adam, peace be upon him. (After Adam, peace be upon him,) the stature of people has continued to decrease."""
"976","It is narrated with the same chain (as previous), the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Paradise is surrounded by disliked things, while Hell is surrounded by desires."""
"977","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those two men cannot be together in Paradise, one of whom said to his Muslim brother, 'O disbeliever.'"""
"978","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""In Paradise, there is a tree under whose shade a rider will travel for a hundred years, but its shade will not end."""
"979","Hasan (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and ‘Awf narrated: I have been informed that it (the shade) will be extended."
"980","With this (previous) chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""By Allah! In Paradise, a place equal to the size of a bow or a whip belonging to any one of you is better than what is between the heavens and the earth."""
"981","It was narrated to us by Ghiyath ibn Bashir, from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz al-Hurmuzi, from Mujahid, who said: It was said to Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, ""Is there hearing in Paradise?"" He said: ""Yes, a tree whose trunk is of gold and its branches are of silver, and its fruit is rubies and emeralds. A wind is sent to it, so it causes some of it to strike against the other, and nothing has ever been heard that is more beautiful than it."""
